-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled programs (sidecars)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Release builds ship these unmodified programs next to the Offbeat binary.
They are downloaded by scripts/fetch-binaries.sh and are not part of this
repository. Their license texts are installed with the app, in the
"licenses" folder of its resources.

  yt-dlp    https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
            The Unlicense (public domain). The standalone build also
            contains Python and other libraries, listed with their licenses
            in YT-DLP-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

  ffmpeg    https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds
  ffprobe   Static "gpl" build of FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), licensed under
            the GNU General Public License v3 or later (FFMPEG-LICENSE.txt).
            FFMPEG-SOURCE.txt names the exact FFmpeg commit of the build.
            Each Offbeat release that ships binaries also attaches the
            corresponding source (ffmpeg-source-*.tar.xz).

  deno      https://github.com/denoland/deno
            MIT License (DENO-LICENSE.md).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Libraries
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Offbeat is built with Tauri (MIT / Apache-2.0), React (MIT) and Lucide (ISC),
among other Rust crates and npm packages. THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, generated
by scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs, lists each one with its license text.

A few crates (cssparser, selectors, dtoa-short, option-ext) are under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0. They are used unmodified, and their source is
available at https://crates.io and in the repositories listed in that file.

The AppImage also carries system libraries from Ubuntu (GTK, WebKitGTK, GLib
and their dependencies, mostly LGPL). They are unmodified, and their source is
available from the Ubuntu archive (https://packages.ubuntu.com, or
`apt-get source <package>`).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Online services
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Offbeat makes no network requests of its own. yt-dlp contacts YouTube to read
and download what the user asks for. When the user turns on the option, it
also queries SponsorBlock (https://sponsor.ajay.app), whose data is licensed
under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Only when the user clicks "Update yt-dlp", yt-dlp's own
updater downloads the latest yt-dlp release from GitHub (https://github.com)
and checks it against the release's SHA-256 list.

